<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>KiTTY++</displayName>
  <description>Group Policy settings of KiTTY++ and its SSH agent kageant.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_KiTTYpp_0_85_1_22">KiTTY++ 0.85.1.22 and later</string>
      <string id="Cat_KiTTYpp">KiTTY++</string>
      <string id="Cat_Store">Settings store</string>
      <string id="Cat_Hardening">Hardening</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent">kageant (SSH agent)</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentKeys">Keys and notifications</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentAccess">Requests from client programs</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentLog">Agent log</string>
      <string id="Cat_KiTTYpp_Rec">KiTTY++ - Default Settings (users can override)</string>
      <string id="Cat_Hardening_Rec">Hardening</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Rec">kageant (SSH agent)</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentKeys_Rec">Keys and notifications</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentAccess_Rec">Requests from client programs</string>
      <string id="Cat_AgentLog_Rec">Agent log</string>
      <string id="SaveMode">Settings store type</string>
      <string id="SaveMode_Help">Specifies where KiTTY++ stores its sessions and settings.

registry: the Windows registry (the default for kitty.exe).
dir: one file per session in the program folder, the portable store (the default for kitty_portable.exe).
file: the registry, with a .sav file imported at startup if the registry key is missing. Legacy mode.

All KiTTY++ programs apply this policy setting, including kitty_portable.exe. The /savemode command and the store buttons are rejected.

Registry value: savemode (REG_SZ).</string>
      <string id="SaveMode_registry">registry</string>
      <string id="SaveMode_dir">dir (portable)</string>
      <string id="SaveMode_file">file (legacy)</string>
      <string id="ReadOnly">Make the settings store read-only</string>
      <string id="ReadOnly_Help">If you enable this policy setting, no KiTTY++ program writes to the settings store. Changes apply to the running process only. Saving a session and the store commands are rejected with &quot;Set by your administrator&quot;.

If you disable this policy setting, the store is writable. A readonly=yes entry in kitty.ini is ignored.

Registry value: readonly (REG_SZ yes or no).</string>
      <string id="KiClassName">Window class name and registry key</string>
      <string id="KiClassName_Help">PuTTY: KiTTY++ registers the PuTTY window class and stores its sessions under the PuTTY registry key (Software\SimonTatham\PuTTY), shared with an installed PuTTY.

If you do not configure this policy setting, KiTTY++ uses its own window class and registry key (Software\kapper.net\KiTTY).

Registry value: KiClassName (REG_SZ).</string>
      <string id="RestrictAcl">Restrict access to KiTTY++ processes</string>
      <string id="RestrictAcl_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kitty.exe and kageant restrict the access rights that other processes of the same user have to them (the process ACL), like the -restrict-acl command-line option.

This policy setting takes precedence over the machine-wide lock an administrator sets in the program (Application &gt; Security &gt; Hardening).

Registry value: restrictacl (REG_SZ yes or no).</string>
      <string id="RestrictAcl_Recommended">Restrict access to KiTTY++ processes</string>
      <string id="RestrictAcl_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kitty.exe and kageant restrict the access rights that other processes of the same user have to them (the process ACL), like the -restrict-acl command-line option.

This policy setting takes precedence over the machine-wide lock an administrator sets in the program (Application &gt; Security &gt; Hardening).

Registry value: restrictacl (REG_SZ yes or no).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="HideApplicationTab">Hide the Application tab</string>
      <string id="HideApplicationTab_Help">If you enable this policy setting, the configuration window has no Application tab. None of its panels is created. -cfgpanel Application/... and the buttons that link to it open the Session tab.

If you disable this policy setting, the tab is shown.

Registry value: applicationsettings (REG_SZ no to hide, yes to show).</string>
      <string id="HideApplicationTab_Recommended">Hide the Application tab</string>
      <string id="HideApplicationTab_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, the configuration window has no Application tab. None of its panels is created. -cfgpanel Application/... and the buttons that link to it open the Session tab.

If you disable this policy setting, the tab is shown.

Registry value: applicationsettings (REG_SZ no to hide, yes to show).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse">Require confirmation for key use</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_Help">Specifies which key uses require confirmation before the key signs.

Keys that request it: only keys whose comment contains &quot;confirmation&quot; (the default).
Every key use: confirmation for each signature.
Never: no confirmation. Requests in key comments are ignored as well. A key set to confirm with Windows Hello still requires confirmation.

Registry value: ConfirmKeyUse (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_ConfirmAuto">Keys that request it</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_ConfirmEvery">Every key use</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_ConfirmNever">Never</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_Recommended">Require confirmation for key use</string>
      <string id="ConfirmKeyUse_Recommended_Help">Specifies which key uses require confirmation before the key signs.

Keys that request it: only keys whose comment contains &quot;confirmation&quot; (the default).
Every key use: confirmation for each signature.
Never: no confirmation. Requests in key comments are ignored as well. A key set to confirm with Windows Hello still requires confirmation.

Registry value: ConfirmKeyUse (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="HelloConfirm">Confirm key use with Windows Hello</string>
      <string id="HelloConfirm_Help">If you enable this policy setting, every key-use confirmation requires Windows Hello verification (biometrics or the device PIN) instead of a Yes button. If Windows Hello is not available, the request is rejected.

Registry value: HelloConfirm (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="HelloConfirm_Recommended">Confirm key use with Windows Hello</string>
      <string id="HelloConfirm_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, every key-use confirmation requires Windows Hello verification (biometrics or the device PIN) instead of a Yes button. If Windows Hello is not available, the request is rejected.

Registry value: HelloConfirm (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyUse">Notify on key use</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyUse_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a notification shows the key after each signature. A key that another program adds or removes triggers a notification that names that program.

Registry value: NotifyOnKeyUse (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyUse_Recommended">Notify on key use</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyUse_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a notification shows the key after each signature. A key that another program adds or removes triggers a notification that names that program.

Registry value: NotifyOnKeyUse (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyArrival">Notify when startup keys become available</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyArrival_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), a notification appears when missing startup keys become available on a drive. The agent log records them in either case.

Registry value: NotifyOnKeyArrival (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyArrival_Recommended">Notify when startup keys become available</string>
      <string id="NotifyOnKeyArrival_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), a notification appears when missing startup keys become available on a drive. The agent log records them in either case.

Registry value: NotifyOnKeyArrival (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="NoticeTimeout">Notification display time</string>
      <string id="NoticeTimeout_Help">The number of seconds kageant's notifications are displayed (2 to 120). If you do not configure this policy setting, each notification uses its own default.

Registry value: NoticeTimeout (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="NoticeTimeout_Recommended">Notification display time</string>
      <string id="NoticeTimeout_Recommended_Help">The number of seconds kageant's notifications are displayed (2 to 120). If you do not configure this policy setting, each notification uses its own default.

Registry value: NoticeTimeout (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="LoadKeysOnStartup">Load remembered keys at startup</string>
      <string id="LoadKeysOnStartup_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kageant loads the remembered key files at startup in encrypted form. The passphrase is required at first use. Only the file paths are stored.

Registry value: LoadKeysOnStartup (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="LoadKeysOnStartup_Recommended">Load remembered keys at startup</string>
      <string id="LoadKeysOnStartup_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kageant loads the remembered key files at startup in encrypted form. The passphrase is required at first use. Only the file paths are stored.

Registry value: LoadKeysOnStartup (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys">Load startup keys from newly attached drives</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_Help">Specifies what kageant does with startup keys that were missing at startup when a drive is attached.

Never: the keys remain missing.
From the stored path: the keys are loaded from their stored drive and path (the default).
From any drive letter: the keys are also searched for at their stored path on the newly attached drive. A key is loaded only if its fingerprint matches the stored one.

Registry value: RetryKeys (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_RetryNever">Never</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_RetryPath">From the stored path</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_RetryAnyDrive">From any drive letter</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_Recommended">Load startup keys from newly attached drives</string>
      <string id="RetryKeys_Recommended_Help">Specifies what kageant does with startup keys that were missing at startup when a drive is attached.

Never: the keys remain missing.
From the stored path: the keys are loaded from their stored drive and path (the default).
From any drive letter: the keys are also searched for at their stored path on the newly attached drive. A key is loaded only if its fingerprint matches the stored one.

Registry value: RetryKeys (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="UnloadOnRemove">Unload keys when their drive is removed</string>
      <string id="UnloadOnRemove_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a key whose drive is removed is unloaded from the agent until the drive is attached again. Disabled by default, so removing a USB drive does not interrupt a login in progress.

Registry value: UnloadOnRemove (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="UnloadOnRemove_Recommended">Unload keys when their drive is removed</string>
      <string id="UnloadOnRemove_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a key whose drive is removed is unloaded from the agent until the drive is attached again. Disabled by default, so removing a USB drive does not interrupt a login in progress.

Registry value: UnloadOnRemove (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="QuietMissingKeys">Suppress notifications for missing startup keys</string>
      <string id="QuietMissingKeys_Help">If you enable this policy setting, no notification appears at startup for startup keys whose drive is not present. A key file that exists but fails to load is still reported.

Registry value: QuietMissingKeys (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="QuietMissingKeys_Recommended">Suppress notifications for missing startup keys</string>
      <string id="QuietMissingKeys_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, no notification appears at startup for startup keys whose drive is not present. A key file that exists but fails to load is still reported.

Registry value: QuietMissingKeys (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="PassphraseCacheSeconds">Passphrase cache time</string>
      <string id="PassphraseCacheSeconds_Help">The number of seconds an entered passphrase is kept, encrypted in memory, to unlock further keys of the same batch (0 to 300, 0 = not cached). Default: 60.

Registry value: PassphraseCacheSeconds (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="PassphraseCacheSeconds_Recommended">Passphrase cache time</string>
      <string id="PassphraseCacheSeconds_Recommended_Help">The number of seconds an entered passphrase is kept, encrypted in memory, to unlock further keys of the same batch (0 to 300, 0 = not cached). Default: 60.

Registry value: PassphraseCacheSeconds (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="HelloCacheSeconds">Windows Hello cache time</string>
      <string id="HelloCacheSeconds_Help">The number of seconds one Windows Hello verification also unlocks further protected keys (0 to 300, 0 = verification each time). Default: 60.

Registry value: HelloCacheSeconds (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="HelloCacheSeconds_Recommended">Windows Hello cache time</string>
      <string id="HelloCacheSeconds_Recommended_Help">The number of seconds one Windows Hello verification also unlocks further protected keys (0 to 300, 0 = verification each time). Default: 60.

Registry value: HelloCacheSeconds (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode">Re-encrypt idle keys</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_Help">Passphrase-protected keys are re-encrypted after the timeout of &quot;Re-encryption timeout&quot;.

Off: no timeout (the default).
Keys without their own timeout: the timeout applies to keys that set none.
All keys: the timeout applies to every key.

Registry value: AutoEncryptMode (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_AutoEncOff">Off</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_AutoEncDefault">Keys without their own timeout</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_AutoEncEnforce">All keys</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_Recommended">Re-encrypt idle keys</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptMode_Recommended_Help">Passphrase-protected keys are re-encrypted after the timeout of &quot;Re-encryption timeout&quot;.

Off: no timeout (the default).
Keys without their own timeout: the timeout applies to keys that set none.
All keys: the timeout applies to every key.

Registry value: AutoEncryptMode (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptSeconds">Re-encryption timeout</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptSeconds_Help">The number of seconds after a key was decrypted or last used for a signature before it is encrypted again: 1 = immediately after each signature, otherwise 30 to 604800 (7 days). Values from 2 to 29 are treated as 30. Default: 600.

Registry value: AutoEncryptSeconds (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptSeconds_Recommended">Re-encryption timeout</string>
      <string id="AutoEncryptSeconds_Recommended_Help">The number of seconds after a key was decrypted or last used for a signature before it is encrypted again: 1 = immediately after each signature, otherwise 30 to 604800 (7 days). Values from 2 to 29 are treated as 30. Default: 600.

Registry value: AutoEncryptSeconds (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows">Action when Windows is locked</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_Help">Specifies what happens to the agent when Windows is locked.

No action (the default).
Lock the agent.
Re-encrypt the keys.

Registry value: LockWithWindows (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_WinLockKeep">No action</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_WinLockLock">Lock the agent</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_WinLockReencrypt">Re-encrypt the keys</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_Recommended">Action when Windows is locked</string>
      <string id="LockWithWindows_Recommended_Help">Specifies what happens to the agent when Windows is locked.

No action (the default).
Lock the agent.
Re-encrypt the keys.

Registry value: LockWithWindows (REG_DWORD 0, 1 or 2).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="ReadKnownHosts">Read the OpenSSH known_hosts file</string>
      <string id="ReadKnownHosts_Help">If you enable this policy setting, %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\known_hosts is a source of host names for the agent log, the confirmation dialog and the rule editor. If you disable this policy setting (the default), kageant never opens the file. KiTTY++ never writes to it.

Registry value: ReadKnownHosts (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="ReadKnownHosts_Recommended">Read the OpenSSH known_hosts file</string>
      <string id="ReadKnownHosts_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\known_hosts is a source of host names for the agent log, the confirmation dialog and the rule editor. If you disable this policy setting (the default), kageant never opens the file. KiTTY++ never writes to it.

Registry value: ReadKnownHosts (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcAdd">Block keys added by client programs</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcAdd_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a key that another program adds is rejected. Together with &quot;Block key removal by client programs&quot;, no program can change the loaded keys. kageant's own buttons are not affected.

Registry value: BlockIpcAdd (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcAdd_Recommended">Block keys added by client programs</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcAdd_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a key that another program adds is rejected. Together with &quot;Block key removal by client programs&quot;, no program can change the loaded keys. kageant's own buttons are not affected.

Registry value: BlockIpcAdd (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcRemove">Block key removal by client programs</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcRemove_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a remove or remove-all request from another program is rejected. Signing and listing keys are not affected.

Registry value: BlockIpcRemove (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcRemove_Recommended">Block key removal by client programs</string>
      <string id="BlockIpcRemove_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, a remove or remove-all request from another program is rejected. Signing and listing keys are not affected.

Registry value: BlockIpcRemove (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AllowIpcLock">Allow client programs to lock the agent</string>
      <string id="AllowIpcLock_Help">If you enable this policy setting, programs can lock and unlock the agent (ssh-add -x and -X). If you disable this policy setting (the default), only the tray menu locks and unlocks it.

Registry value: AllowIpcLock (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AllowIpcLock_Recommended">Allow client programs to lock the agent</string>
      <string id="AllowIpcLock_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, programs can lock and unlock the agent (ssh-add -x and -X). If you disable this policy setting (the default), only the tray menu locks and unlocks it.

Registry value: AllowIpcLock (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="BlockForwardedChanges">Block changes through agent forwarding</string>
      <string id="BlockForwardedChanges_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), add, remove, lock and unlock requests from a program on a server the agent is forwarded to are rejected. Listing and signing are not affected. A connection counts as forwarded only if its client sends session-bind marked for forwarding.

Registry value: BlockForwardedChanges (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="BlockForwardedChanges_Recommended">Block changes through agent forwarding</string>
      <string id="BlockForwardedChanges_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), add, remove, lock and unlock requests from a program on a server the agent is forwarded to are rejected. Listing and signing are not affected. A connection counts as forwarded only if its client sends session-bind marked for forwarding.

Registry value: BlockForwardedChanges (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AllowWmCopyData">Allow requests by window messages</string>
      <string id="AllowWmCopyData_Help">If you enable this policy setting, requests by window messages (WM_COPYDATA) are accepted. Programs built on PuTTY before 0.75 connect to the agent this way. kageant cannot identify the program that sends such a request. If you disable this policy setting (the default), they are rejected.

Registry value: AllowWmCopyData (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AllowWmCopyData_Recommended">Allow requests by window messages</string>
      <string id="AllowWmCopyData_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, requests by window messages (WM_COPYDATA) are accepted. Programs built on PuTTY before 0.75 connect to the agent this way. kageant cannot identify the program that sends such a request. If you disable this policy setting (the default), they are rejected.

Registry value: AllowWmCopyData (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="OpenSSHPipe">Serve the Windows OpenSSH agent pipe</string>
      <string id="OpenSSHPipe_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kageant also serves \\.\pipe\openssh-ssh-agent for ssh.exe, ssh-add and other OpenSSH clients. If another program already owns that pipe, kageant serves only its own pipe.

Registry value: OpenSSHPipe (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="OpenSSHPipe_Recommended">Serve the Windows OpenSSH agent pipe</string>
      <string id="OpenSSHPipe_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, kageant also serves \\.\pipe\openssh-ssh-agent for ssh.exe, ssh-add and other OpenSSH clients. If another program already owns that pipe, kageant serves only its own pipe.

Registry value: OpenSSHPipe (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="ExtraPipe">Additional named pipe</string>
      <string id="ExtraPipe_Help">An additional pipe name that kageant serves as \\.\pipe\&lt;name&gt;. The name persists across restarts. Allowed characters: letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-', up to 200.

Registry value: ExtraPipe (REG_SZ).</string>
      <string id="ExtraPipe_Recommended">Additional named pipe</string>
      <string id="ExtraPipe_Recommended_Help">An additional pipe name that kageant serves as \\.\pipe\&lt;name&gt;. The name persists across restarts. Allowed characters: letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-', up to 200.

Registry value: ExtraPipe (REG_SZ).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="SetSshAuthSock">Set SSH_AUTH_SOCK</string>
      <string id="SetSshAuthSock_Help">If you enable this policy setting, the user's SSH_AUTH_SOCK environment variable points to the additional named pipe. Programs started afterwards use it. A value set by someone else is not overwritten.

Registry value: SetSshAuthSock (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="SetSshAuthSock_Recommended">Set SSH_AUTH_SOCK</string>
      <string id="SetSshAuthSock_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting, the user's SSH_AUTH_SOCK environment variable points to the additional named pipe. Programs started afterwards use it. A value set by someone else is not overwritten.

Registry value: SetSshAuthSock (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLog">Enable the agent log</string>
      <string id="AgentLog_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), kageant records what it does with keys, as signed and chained entries, at the destination set by &quot;Agent log destination&quot;.

Registry value: AgentLog (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AgentLog_Recommended">Enable the agent log</string>
      <string id="AgentLog_Recommended_Help">If you enable this policy setting (the default), kageant records what it does with keys, as signed and chained entries, at the destination set by &quot;Agent log destination&quot;.

Registry value: AgentLog (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLogPath">Agent log file path</string>
      <string id="AgentLogPath_Help">The full path of the log file. If you do not configure this policy setting: next to kitty.ini for a portable copy, otherwise %LOCALAPPDATA%\kapper.net\KiTTY\kageant.log. Environment variables are not expanded.

Registry value: AgentLogPath (REG_SZ).</string>
      <string id="AgentLogPath_Recommended">Agent log file path</string>
      <string id="AgentLogPath_Recommended_Help">The full path of the log file. If you do not configure this policy setting: next to kitty.ini for a portable copy, otherwise %LOCALAPPDATA%\kapper.net\KiTTY\kageant.log. Environment variables are not expanded.

Registry value: AgentLogPath (REG_SZ).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink">Agent log destination</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_Help">File, Windows Event Log, or both. If you do not configure this policy setting: both if the KiTTY++_Agent event log exists (an all-users installation), otherwise the file.

Registry value: AgentLogSink (REG_SZ).</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_SinkFile">File</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_SinkEventLog">Windows Event Log</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_SinkBoth">File and Windows Event Log</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_Recommended">Agent log destination</string>
      <string id="AgentLogSink_Recommended_Help">File, Windows Event Log, or both. If you do not configure this policy setting: both if the KiTTY++_Agent event log exists (an all-users installation), otherwise the file.

Registry value: AgentLogSink (REG_SZ).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLogMaxKB">Maximum log file size</string>
      <string id="AgentLogMaxKB_Help">The size in KB at which the log file is rotated (16 to 1048576). Default: 5120.

Registry value: AgentLogMaxKB (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AgentLogMaxKB_Recommended">Maximum log file size</string>
      <string id="AgentLogMaxKB_Recommended_Help">The size in KB at which the log file is rotated (16 to 1048576). Default: 5120.

Registry value: AgentLogMaxKB (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLogKeep">Number of rotated files to keep</string>
      <string id="AgentLogKeep_Help">The number of rotated log files to keep (1 to 99). Default: 3.

Registry value: AgentLogKeep (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AgentLogKeep_Recommended">Number of rotated files to keep</string>
      <string id="AgentLogKeep_Recommended_Help">The number of rotated log files to keep (1 to 99). Default: 3.

Registry value: AgentLogKeep (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
      <string id="AgentLogExpireDays">Rotated file retention</string>
      <string id="AgentLogExpireDays_Help">The number of days after which rotated log files are deleted at the next rotation (0 to 3650, 0 = never deleted). Default: 90.

Registry value: AgentLogExpireDays (REG_DWORD).</string>
      <string id="AgentLogExpireDays_Recommended">Rotated file retention</string>
      <string id="AgentLogExpireDays_Recommended_Help">The number of days after which rotated log files are deleted at the next rotation (0 to 3650, 0 = never deleted). Default: 90.

Registry value: AgentLogExpireDays (REG_DWORD).

Recommended policy: applies while the user has no value of their own. The mandatory policy of the same name under &quot;KiTTY++&quot; overrides it.</string>
    </stringTable>
